The number of cascade rounds and the value of `size` (3 or 4 bytes per round) are controlled entirely by the peer device via the cascade tag and cascade-incomplete bit. The driver appends data to `target->nfcid1` without checking if the total length would exceed the allocated buffer (`NFC_NFCID1_MAXSIZE = 10`), enabling a malicious peer to cause a heap buffer overflow.

